/-!
# The completion functor is idempotent on the unit, and Tag 099B

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site and let `f_1, …, f_r` be global sections of `𝒪`. The completion
functor of [Stacks, Tag 099B] is `Φ K = K^∧ = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), K)` and the completion map is
`η_K : K ⟶ K^∧`, both built in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/DerivedCompletionRinged/Completion.lean`. That
file reduces the conclusion for the ideal sheaf `(f_1, …, f_r)` to three properties of
`(Φ, η)`, listed there as clauses 1, 2 and 3 of "What remains for Tag 099B"; clause 2 is
`CompletionUnitIso.lean`. This file proves **clauses 1 and 3**, and so **closes
[Stacks, Tag 099B]**: the inclusion `D_comp(𝒪) ⥤ D(𝒪)` has a left adjoint along the ideal sheaf
generated by `f_1, …, f_r`, and `Φ` is it.

The computation is the source's: for a global section `g` in which one of the `f_j` becomes a
unit,

`R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_g, K^∧) = R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_g ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 Č(f), K) = 0`,

because `𝒪_g ⊗_𝒪 Č(f)` is the extended alternating Čech complex of the images of `f_1, …, f_r`
in `𝒪_g`, where `f_j` is invertible, hence contractible.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.tensorAwayExtendedAlternatingCechIso`: the degreewise tensor
  product `Č(f) ⊗_𝒪 𝒪_g` is the extended alternating Čech complex of the base-changed
  localization system `S ↦ 𝒪_{f_S} ⊗_𝒪 𝒪_g`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_Q_tensorAwayModule_extendedAlternatingCech_of_isUnit`:
  `Č(f) ⊗_𝒪 𝒪_g` is a zero object of `D(𝒪)` when some `f_j` becomes a unit in `𝒪_g`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.memVanishingIdeal_completionFunctor_of_isUnit`: consequently
  `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪_g, K^∧) = 0` for every `K`, which is condition (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0997] for
  `K^∧` at `g`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.memVanishingIdeal_prodGlobalSection_completionFunctor`: the same
  at `g = f_S` for every non-empty `S ⊆ {1, …, r}`, with no hypothesis at all.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_completionFunctor`: **clause 1 of
  [Stacks, Tag 099B]**, that `K^∧` is derived complete along `(f_1, …, f_r)`, with no hypothesis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_completionFunctor_obj`: therefore
  `η_{K^∧}` is invertible — clause 2 at a completion, with no derived-completeness input.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_completionFunctor_map_completionUnit_app`: **`Φ η_K` is
  invertible**, with no hypothesis. This is the hypothesis `hΦη` of
  `Stacks.Algebraization.isRightAdjoint_ι_of_completionFunctor`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor_map_completionUnit_app`: **clause 3 of
  [Stacks, Tag 099B]**, `Φ η_K = η_{Φ K}`, granted clause 1.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_isDerivedComplete_completion`
  and
  `RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections_of_isDerivedComplete`:
  the conclusion for this ideal sheaf, granted clause 1.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.bijective_precomp_completionUnit_idealOfGlobalSections`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 099B], with no hypothesis left** — the inclusion
  `D_comp(𝒪) ⥤ D(𝒪)` has a left adjoint for `ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r)`, and that adjoint is the Čech
  completion `K ↦ R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(Č(f), K)`.

## Implementation notes

**Where the contractibility comes from.** `Č(f) ⊗_𝒪 𝒪_g` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.extendedAlternatingCech` of the system
`S ↦ 𝒪_{f_S} ⊗_𝒪 𝒪_g` by `Stacks.Sheaves.CechFlatNeighbourhood.tensorExtendedAlternatingCechIso`
— the tensor endofunctor is additive and, `𝒪_g` being flat
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isFlat_awayModule`), preserves the finite products that form the
terms. That system is the system of localizations of `𝒪_g` by
`Stacks.Sheaves.CechFlatNeighbourhood.awayLocalizationBaseChangeIso`, *naturally in `S`*, which
is what makes its transition maps the ones
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_awayModuleTransition_of_subset_insert` is about. So the
contracting homotopy of `CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.isZero_Q_complex` applies to the
system directly, and neither the sectionwise base change nor a complex-level comparison of the
two Čech complexes is needed.

**From the degreewise to the derived tensor product.** The currying isomorphism of
[Stacks, Tag 08J9] produces `𝒪_g[0] ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 Č(f)`, with the localization on the *left*. The
K-flat bridge `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedTensorSingleAwayModuleIso` of
`AwayKFlat.lean` computes it with the localization on the right, so the commutativity
constraint `Stacks.DerivedTensor.RingedSite.DerivedTensorProduct.braidingIso` of
[Stacks, Tag 0FPT] is interposed; it is read at the canonical derived tensor product of the
ringed site through `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedTensorProductDatumOfSite`, the two
packagings of [Stacks, Tag 06YU] carrying the same bifunctor.

**Why clause 3 does not need the two multiplications of `Č(f)` to agree.** Under currying,
`Φ η_K` and `η_{Φ K}` are the two maps `R𝑆heafHom(Č, K) ⟶ R𝑆heafHom(Č ⊗^𝐋 Č, K)` induced by
`1 ⊗ a` and `a ⊗ 1`, and comparing them directly would be a statement about the algebra
structure of `Č(f)`. It is not needed: `Stacks.Algebraization.bijective_precomp_completionUnit`
of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/DerivedCompletion.lean` asks only for
*invertibility* of `Φ η_K`, and the equality then follows from the injectivity half of that
bijection applied to the naturality square of `η` at `η_K` itself. Invertibility of `Φ η_K` is
proved here the way clause 2 proves invertibility of `η_K`: the filtration triangle
`Č^{≥1} ⟶ Č^{≥0} ⟶ Č⁰[0]` is pushed through `R𝑆heafHom(-, K)` and then through
`Φ = R𝑆heafHom(Č, -)` — the covariant half of [Stacks, Tag 08JC],
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_distinguished_derivedSheafHom_second` — and its third
vertex `Φ(R𝑆heafHom(Č^{≥1}, K))` vanishes because currying twice and braiding once identify it
with `R𝑆heafHom(Č^{≥1}, Φ K)`, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isZero_derivedSheafHom_stupidTruncGE_one` at `Φ K`, whose
hypothesis is `memVanishingIdeal_prodGlobalSection_completionFunctor`.

**How clause 1 reaches the per-slice predicate.** `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete`
of [Stacks, Tag 0999] is a condition *per slice* — for every object `V` the restriction
`(K^∧)|_V` must satisfy the Milnor condition at `f_i|_V` — while
`memVanishingIdeal_prodGlobalSection_completionFunctor` is that condition over `𝒞` itself. The
passage between them is the *descent* direction, which is free: derived restriction to a slice
is additive, preserves the countable products of the derived categories
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.preservesProducts_mapDerivedCategory_overFunctor`) and carries
multiplication by a global section to multiplication by its value on the slice
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.overFunctor_map_globalSectionToEnd`), so it transports the invertibility
of the Milnor difference by `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedCompleteAt_map_of_smul_id`.
That is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedCompleteAtSection_of_isDerivedCompleteAt` of
`CompleteGlobalSection.lean`, the converse of the ascent
`isDerivedCompleteAt_of_forall_isDerivedCompleteAtSection` which clause 2 consumes and which,
going the other way, does need the locality of invertibility in `D(𝒪)`.

In particular **neither [Stacks, Tag 08JB] nor an identification `Č(f)|_V ≅ Č(f|_V)` is used**:
the Čech complex never has to be recognised on a slice, because the vanishing is established
over `𝒞` and only then restricted. The route through 08JB — restricting the derived internal
Hom as in the proof of [Stacks, Tag 099A], and recognising `(K^∧)|_V` as the completion of
`K|_V` over the slice ringed site — would need the naturality in `S` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.awayModuleProdOverIso`, which is not proved; [Stacks, Tag 099E]
does not need it (`FiniteTypeExtendedCech.lean`).

**Tag 099F.** The source states that proposition for an arbitrary *finite type* sheaf of ideals,
one only locally generated by finitely many sections. Everything here is for an ideal sheaf
generated by finitely many *global* sections, which is the hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 099B] and
not of [Stacks, Tag 099F]; so the `@[stacks 099B]` attribute is attached below and no
`@[stacks 099F]` attribute is. The tag is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete` of `FiniteTypeReflector.lean`,
through the map
`K ⟶ 𝒪` of [Stacks, Tag 099E].

